test_frag — IPv4 egress fragmentation self-test
================================================

First half of Option B (post-Phase 4 deferred queue priority #1):
RFC 791 §3.2 IP fragmentation on the egress UDP path. Inet now
consults a per-destination PMTU cache before deciding whether
to send a UDP datagram as a single IP packet or split it into
fragments.

This test seeds the PMTU cache for the limited-broadcast address
(skips ARP, so the test runs without depending on slirp ARP
state), reads the running fragment-egress counter before and
after a 1000-byte sendto, and asserts the delta matches the
expected fragment count.

Math (PMTU=300, dlen=1000):

- IP payload size = UDP header(8) + data(1000) = 1008 bytes.
- Per-fragment IP-payload = ((300 - 20) / 8) * 8 = 280 bytes.
- N = ceil(1008 / 280) = 4 (sizes 280, 280, 280, 168).

Pass criterion: prints `test_frag: ok`.

    module oskit.bin.test_frag

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with}
    import oskit.net.{socket, sendto, close_socket,
        pmtu_inject_test, frag_egress_count}
    import std.net.{AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM, ipv4}


    print_idec(v: int)
        var n = v
        if n < 0
            puts("-")
            n = -n
        if n >= 10
            print_idec(n / 10)
        var b: [1]byte
        b[0] = byte('0' + (n % 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 1))


    fail(code: int)
        puts("test_frag: failed ")
        print_idec(code)
        puts("\n")
        exit_with(code)


    main(argv: []string)
        val fd = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM, 0)
        if fd < 0
            fail(1)
            return

Seed PMTU=300 for the broadcast destination. We use broadcast to
sidestep ARP — sendto to a unicast destination would need the
gateway MAC resolved, which depends on slirp timing. Broadcast
just emits to ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff with IP src forced to 0.0.0.0
(RFC 2131 §4.1) and the cache lookup still fires for the
all-ones address.

        if pmtu_inject_test(255, 255, 255, 255, 300) != 0
            close_socket(fd)
            fail(2)
            return

        val before = frag_egress_count()
        if before < 0
            close_socket(fd)
            fail(3)
            return

        var payload: [1000]byte
        var i = 0
        while i < 1000
            payload[i] = byte((i & 0xff))
            i += 1

        val sent = sendto(fd, &payload[0], 1000, ipv4(255, 255, 255, 255), 9000)
        if sent != 1000
            close_socket(fd)
            fail(4)
            return

        val after = frag_egress_count()
        if after < 0
            close_socket(fd)
            fail(5)
            return

        val delta = after - before
        if delta != 4
            puts("test_frag: expected 4 frags, got ")
            print_idec(delta)
            puts("\n")
            close_socket(fd)
            fail(6)
            return

        close_socket(fd)
        puts("test_frag: ok\n")
        exit()
